# API tests

Vitest API/unit/integration tests for active `@ethereumjs/*` libraries. Consensus runners and benchmarks are out of scope here.

## Scope

**In scope:** each package's `test/` tree (for VM: `test/api/` only).

**Out of scope:**

- VM consensus runners: `packages/vm/test/tester/**` (legacy state/blockchain, EST)
- Benchmarks: `test/bench/`, `test/benchmark/`
- Deprecated packages (`client`, `devp2p`, `ethash`, `wallet`) — containment only per `security.mdc`

**Special-care runners** (do not delete or weaken without explicit intent):

- `packages/tx/test/transactionRunner.spec.ts`, `t9n.spec.ts` (ethereum-tests submodule; fork-split scripts)
- `packages/mpt/test/official.spec.ts`, `packages/rlp/test/official.spec.ts`
- EVM EOF/submodule readers under `packages/evm/test/eips/`
- VM `test/api/tester/**` (diagnostic helpers, not consensus)

After test edits: `npm run tsc` in touched packages, spellcheck on touched files (`typecheck.mdc`, `spellcheck.mdc`).

## Directory layout

**Default:** flat `test/<area>.spec.ts` aligned with `src/` modules.

**Use subdirs when justified:**

| Pattern | Example | When |
|---------|---------|------|
| Mirror `src/` subtree | `mpt/test/trie/`, `util/test/bal/` | Package has distinct subsystems |
| Fixture dirs | `block/test/testdata/`, `rlp/test/fixture/` | Large static vectors |
| Shared helpers | `tx/test/testData/`, `tx/txTypeMatrix.ts` | Cross-spec constants |
| EIP-scoped specs | `eip1559.spec.ts`, `vm/test/api/EIPs/` | EIP-only behavior not shared across types |
| Official runners | `official.spec.ts`, `transactionRunner.spec.ts` | Submodule / vendored vectors |

Do not force 1:1 `src/` ↔ `test/` when types share capabilities (tx is the reference: matrix + EIP files).

## File naming and renames

- Spec files: `*.spec.ts`
- **Renames:** always `git mv old new` — never delete + recreate. Update imports in the same commit (`git.mdc`).
- **Module-aligned:** `<module>.spec.ts` (`bytes.spec.ts`, `header.spec.ts`)
- **EIP-scoped:** `eipNNNN.spec.ts` — no redundant suffixes
- **Integration / RPC:** pick one style per package and stay consistent within that package
- **Official vectors:** `official.spec.ts` or `<domain>Runner.spec.ts`

## describe / it naming

- **describe:** bracketed scope tag — `[Common]: Hardfork logic`, `[LegacyTx]`, `[RLP]: encode`
  - Multi-type files: list types in the tag
  - Subsystems: nest describes (`MapDB` → `get`)
- **it:** name the function or behavior under test — `'ecrecover() rejects invalid v'`, not leftover names from other packages
- **Official vector loops:** one `it` per vector when failures must pinpoint a case (rlp); batched single `it` when startup cost dominates (mpt official) — do not regress wall time when splitting

## Shared helpers and fixtures

Reuse order:

1. Local `test/helpers.ts`, `test/utils.ts`, or `<feature>Matrix.ts`
2. `@ethereumjs/testdata` for cross-package chain configs, genesis, blocks, signers, BAL vectors
3. Package-local `test/testdata/` for large domain fixtures not yet generic enough
4. Submodules (`ethereum-tests`) only in dedicated runner specs — never in shared matrices

**Matrix pattern** (reference: `packages/tx/test/txTypeMatrix.ts`): export shared constants, stub crypto, invalid-input tables; drive cross-variant tests with a typed array + `for` loop in base-style specs; EIP files hold only what the matrix cannot express.

## Coverage expectations

- Logic coverage alone is insufficient for **S0** paths — see `security.mdc` (wrong JS inputs on fee/value/nonce and similar guard rails)
- Prefer testing public API (`createX`, factories, serializers) over private helpers
- Close obvious gaps: uncovered error paths, alternate constructors, freeze/opt-out
- Do not weaken or skip official vectors to raise coverage

## Performance

- Do not slow the default suite during restructure
- Isolate expensive setup (real KZG/WASM/crypto) in dedicated specs with long `beforeAll` timeout; stub in shared matrices (`security.mdc` EIP-4844 note)
- Keep env-specific tests in package `vitest.config.browser.mts` exclude lists
- Keep official runner fork splits, batched loops, and CI exclusions
- Prefer pre-baked TS fixtures over disk walks in hot paths

## Vitest mechanics

- `describe` / `it` + `assert` from `vitest`
- Manual `for` loops over tables preferred over `it.each` (tx pattern)
- `describe.skipIf(isBrowser)` for Node-only tests
- Typecheck includes `test/` — guard union types in matrix loops

Tx-specific matrix, KZG, and runner rules: `tx-tests.mdc`.
